                        "review": "This game feels like they took elements from various other indie roguelikes and classic zombie flash games, without giving themselves time to actually flesh out and/or polish any of these aspects.\n\nThe movement is very ill-equipped for in-the-moment action. It plays like a Death Road To Canada ripoff that had it's movement system and visibility kneecapped at the last minute so they can advertise it as an \"RTS\". Enemies can and will jump you due to the fog-of-war. The thing with the movement is that even at the best of times, it's very clunky. You have no direct control of your characters, merely being able to command them to move to a spot or tell them to do a thing. At the worst of times, an enemy will jump you and in the ensuing commotion the pathfinding or the movement speed may end up screwing you over. I'm not entirely convinced that the infinite revive system wasn't implemented as a band-aid to mitigate the glaring movement issues.\n\nDuring exploration segments, you will find yourself clicking constantly due to the screen being way too zoomed in. Befuddlingly enough, they give you free range to take control of either the entire group at once, or just one character at a time. It feels like the remnants of a scrapped turn-based system, since with how the game is designed it'd be very disorienting keeping track of multiple characters all on different sides across a given map in real time.\nAlso, as a small nitpick: your characters have varying movements speeds to where some of them will lag, and others will speed ahead of the group.\n\nThe tower defense (AKA \"scouting\") aspect feels half-baked. It's actually rather broken since the turrets are much more powerful than your own squad. But as far as I can tell there's no alternate structures and the level layouts are so bite-sized there's little wiggle room for actual strategy. Build at least one tower, or if you can't afford to, huddle your bois up.\n\nThe good parts of the game come from the non-action bits. I like the base building stuff, and the city map feels very Rebuild. Sadly there's not quite as much random-gen as I was expecting.\n\nI'm just very glad I got this at a steep discount. I'd refund the hell out of this if I bought it at full price. If you have a tolerance for jank and can find it on sale (this describes me), then ig go for it.\n\nAlso quick shoutout to the fucking hitscan human enemies the game can just decide to throw at you lol",
